# Copy to .env (never commit .env). Guide §4.2
SAP_URL=https://ihr-testsystem.example.com
SAP_USERNAME=TEST_AUTOMATION
SAP_PASSWORD=bitte-aendern

# Ariba (guide §4.5 / §7.4) – optional. Each system in systems.json has its three variables here.
ARIBA_URL=
ARIBA_USER=
ARIBA_PASS=

# Optional: use an already-installed Chromium instead of `npx playwright install`
# CHROMIUM_PATH=/opt/pw-browsers/chromium

# Optional: an SAP trial system with a self-signed certificate, e.g. a Cloud Appliance Library
# appliance reached by its IP. Host only. While SAP_URL is on this host, the SAP-login systems'
# browsers skip the certificate check, for every address they reach; other systems never do
# (README, "A trial system with a self-signed certificate").
# SAP_SELF_SIGNED_HOST=203.0.113.10

# OData tests (tests/api, sap-plugin/odata.ts) – optional, the tests are skipped without them.
# Host only, no path. They create and change data there: use a development or trial system on
# which the service GWSAMPLE_BASIC is active (/IWFND/MAINT_SERVICE).
SAP_API_URL=
SAP_API_USERNAME=
SAP_API_PASSWORD=
# SAP_CLIENT=002

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mocks: Mock IDoc and Mock PLC – optional, all of them. Without them the mocks run on this
# computer only, which is all the tests and a first try need. Fill them in to connect SAP.
#
# Where a value takes effect:
# - The tests read this file (playwright.config.ts loads it). The local receiver and Mock PLC
#   they start (`bun run test:idoc`, `bun run test:mfs`) ignore the settings here and stay on
#   this computer.
# - The receiver's settings (IDOC_HOST to IDOC_PASSWORD): the app takes them from its own
#   environment, else from this file, and starts the receiver on the Mock IDoc page with them.
# - The Mock PLC's MFS_HOST and MFS_BASE_PORT: the app takes them from its own environment only.
# - Values marked "app": the app reads them from its own environment only.
# - On the command line (`bun run idoc:server`, `bun run mfs:server`): set them in the shell.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# IDoc receiver (idoc/, the Mock IDoc page; see idoc/README.md). SAP posts IDocs to
# https://<IDOC_HOST>:<IDOC_PORT>/idoc/<partner> through an SM59 type G destination and a WE21
# XML HTTP port. Beyond this computer the receiver needs HTTPS and a login, or it won't start.
# IDOC_HOST=0.0.0.0
# IDOC_PORT=47200
# Server certificate and key (PEM files). Test ones: `bun run idoc:certs <host>`.
# IDOC_TLS_CERT=idoc/certs/server.pem
# IDOC_TLS_KEY=idoc/certs/server.key
# Login, either a user and password (the destination's logon data) ...
# IDOC_USER=
# IDOC_PASSWORD=
# ... or SAP's client certificate: the CA that signed it, and its SHA-256 fingerprint
# (openssl x509 -noout -fingerprint -sha256 -in sap-client.pem). Set both logins, and SAP needs both.
# IDOC_TLS_CA=
# IDOC_TLS_CLIENT_FINGERPRINT=
# A receiver that runs elsewhere (on the cluster): the address of its control API and its token.
# Tests use it through the idocInbox fixture; the app controls it (app).
# IDOC_HUB_URL=https://idoc-mock.example.com:47201
# IDOC_HUB_TOKEN=

# Sending IDocs into SAP through the receiver, as SAP Cloud Integration does (idoc/README.md,
# "Sending into SAP"): one set per system, IDOC_S4_* for S/4HANA and IDOC_EWM_* for EWM. The
# address, client, user and password can also be saved on the Settings page; tests never get
# them, only the receiver does. A system without an address gets a stand-in in the receiver.
# IDOC_S4_URL=https://s4dev.example.com:44300
# IDOC_S4_CLIENT=100
# IDOC_S4_USER=
# IDOC_S4_PASSWORD=
# IDOC_EWM_URL=https://ewmdev.example.com:44300
# IDOC_EWM_CLIENT=100
# IDOC_EWM_USER=
# IDOC_EWM_PASSWORD=
# Per system, also: _SERVICE (soap or xml), _TLS_CERT and _TLS_KEY (a client certificate instead
# of or besides the user), _TLS_CA (a CA for SAP's server certificate), _TIMEOUT_MS.
# No stand-ins: IDOC_FAKE_SAP=0

# Importing test cases from OpenText Octane (the app's "Import from Octane" page). The server without
# /ui, and the shared space and workspace: the two numbers after ?p= in a link to Octane. An API
# access key of that workspace (Settings > Spaces > API access in Octane), with a role that can read
# tests. Also on the Settings page; only the app reads them, test runs never get them.
# OCTANE_URL=https://octane.example.com
# OCTANE_SHARED_SPACE=1001
# OCTANE_WORKSPACE=1002
# OCTANE_CLIENT_ID=
# OCTANE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Mock PLC (mfs/, the Mock PLC page; see mfs/README.md). EWM connects to the PLC ports: one per
# PLC, from MFS_BASE_PORT on. The EWM communication channels must point to MFS_HOST.
# Address and first port of the PLCs (app: mode "Wait for EWM").
# MFS_HOST=0.0.0.0
# MFS_BASE_PORT=47101
# The warehouse setup in mfs/setups, for `bun run mfs:server` (the app asks on its page).
# MFS_SETUP=sap-example
# A Mock PLC that runs elsewhere: its control API and token. Tests use it through the mfs
# fixture; the app controls it (app).
# MFS_EMULATOR_URL=https://mock-plc.example.com:47100
# MFS_EMULATOR_TOKEN=
